Z||000000||Johnson's85SE||11-30-2001||02:44 PM||||Hey guys, <BR> Its winter time again up here in Calgary. I just want to no the symtums of a bad heater core, and a bad thermistat. I have changed both within the 2 years. My car doesn't overheat. It just never really gets hot. My rad fan is off always. the hot/cold thing is changing. What do you guys think?  <P>------------------<BR>80's Import killer.<BR>[img]C:\My Documents\Stuff\Sports Cars\85fiero.bmp[/img]||||reg||1
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||11-30-2001||02:52 PM||||Sounds more like something else...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>The telltale sign of a heater core gone bad is antifreeze smell, which tends to fog up windshield with slimy vapor when defroster is on.<P>The thermostat, usually if its stuck, won't open up and let coolant flow. This makes the temp go way up...<P>Maybe your temp gauge???<P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed<BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red & shiny all over - with all the options!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||11-30-2001||03:11 PM||||Thermostat could also stick open and not let the car get hot enough.  If you have a low temp thermostat go to the 195 degree stat to get the engine hotter.||||reg||1
